==English==

===Etymology===
From {{enm|en|en}} {{term|ulage|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|xno}} {{term|ullage|lang=xno}}, from {{recons|ullier|ullier|to fill a partially empty cask|lang=xno}}, from {{etyl|fro}} {{term|oel||lang=fro|bunghole", literally, "eye}}, from {{etyl|la}} {{term|oculus||lang=la|eye}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|-}}

# In a wine bottle, the empty space between the cork and the top of the wine.
# In a cask or barrel, the empty space, occupied by air, that is created by not completely filling the cask or barrel
# In an industrial setting, the empty space in a tank, such as for fuel

